# ⛔ THIS FILE IS THE PIN POLICY, and it is a WHITELIST, not a blocklist.
#
# This directory is mounted as a submodule INSIDE a working tree that also
# holds build directories nobody pins any more — historical builds that are
# still reachable locally by `SEEDLING_PAGE=<name>` and must stay on disk
# without ever being committed here. A blocklist cannot express that: a new
# historical build would silently become trackable. So everything is ignored
# and each PINNED build is named back in, one line each.
#
# THE RULE: a build is pinned iff a TRACKED file of PeerInfinity/Archipelago-CC
# names it. That repo's scripts/procgen/check-seedling-wasm-pins.mjs gates the
# agreement between this whitelist, builds.json, and what git tracks here, so
# adding a line without the manifest entry (or vice versa) reds a CI row.
#
# ⚖ AND SINCE 2026-09-07 THE RULE HAS A SECOND CLAUSE (user ruling 4): a build
# may also be pinned as a DEMO — `demo: true` in its builds.json entry PLUS a
# link to `<name>/game.html` in the README below. Nothing in Archipelago-CC
# names `seedling_original`, and nothing should: it is the game a person plays,
# not a build an instrument drives. The README link is the load-bearing half —
# `demo: true` alone would be the manifest admitting itself — and the gate
# prints which of the two reasons admitted each build on every run.
#
# To ADD a build:    a `!/<name>/` line here + a builds.json entry + the dir.
# To RETIRE one:     delete both; the directory may stay on disk, untracked.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/builds.json

# ── the pinned builds ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/seedling_bot_ap_p4b/
!/seedling_bot_ap_p4c/
!/seedling_bot_ap_p4d/

# ── the demo build (⚖ ruling 4: `demo: true` + the README link) ──────────
!/seedling_original/
